WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.377 --> 00:00:04.115
♫ La la la la la la la la la

00:00:04.115 --> 00:00:07.906
♫ la la la la la la ♫

00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:13.349
(comical detective music)

00:00:15.016 --> 00:00:16.235
- [Voiceover] How often do
you have a random thought

00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:18.255
and think, "Where did that come from?"

00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:20.937
Chances are it's not as
random as you might think.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:23.073
Your thoughts are influenced
by information that is obtained

00:00:23.073 --> 00:00:25.034
from the world around you and filtered

00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:26.858
through all of your past memories.

00:00:26.858 --> 00:00:29.238
Sometimes thoughts that
may seem completely random

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:31.316
could actually be your mind
unconsciously recalling

00:00:31.316 --> 00:00:34.089
information that is closely
linked in your memory.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:37.341
For example, if your friend
asks you to name a random fruit

00:00:37.341 --> 00:00:38.815
while at the same time
they're talking about their

00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:42.262
brand new yellow car and their
matching yellow driving cab,

00:00:42.262 --> 00:00:44.735
your brain is primed with the word yellow.

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:47.383
So even though there's a
wide variety of fruits,

00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:50.297
you're more likely to
jump to the word banana.

00:00:50.297 --> 00:00:55.063
(comical detective music)

00:01:09.882 --> 00:01:12.222
- Okay, go?

00:01:14.851 --> 00:01:17.770
- She held the feather.

00:01:21.016 --> 00:01:22.861
- Number one, he ate the banana.

00:01:22.861 --> 00:01:24.394
- She held the feather.

00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:26.112
- The dog loves benches.

00:01:26.112 --> 00:01:27.877
- She has webbed feet.

00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:29.316
- Crumbs are never left.

00:01:29.316 --> 00:01:30.639
- The kids were swimming.

00:01:30.639 --> 00:01:32.271
- The sun is hot.

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:34.346
Sophia.

00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:36.734
An animal?
